>  1a. ...If the PC has MR?

Magic resistance doesn't protect against death field explosion damage.
Being polymorphed into a non-living monster or a demon does.

>  1b. Does this effect have to pass an MC check?

No. MC is irrelevant to anything that isn't a monster's special melee
attack.

> 2. Does this effect happen if the wand is *blown up by electric shock* 
> instead of *broken by <a>pplying*?

Not in vanilla: it will just do the d10 damage that any wand does
exploding in this manner. No such explosions cause any wand effects.

[2bis. Does this effect happen if the wand explodes from overcharging?]

No: that does d(2/3 max HP) damage, regardless of wand type, no wand
effects.

